---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { PRIVACY_EMAIL, SUPPORT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---
<Legal
  pageTitle={`Privacy Policy | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} collects, uses, and protects information across its products, including application and integration data.`}
>
  <p>
    I build and operate software including Toolport, Toolport Teams, and the Omarchy plugins published on
    this site. This policy explains the types of information these services may collect, how it is used, and
    how to contact me.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on the product, we may collect account information, contact details, product usage data,
    uploaded files, support messages, billing status, and technical information needed to operate and secure the service.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <p>
    We use information to provide the service, process support requests, improve product reliability,
    protect accounts, communicate important updates, and comply with legal obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Application &amp; Integration Data</h2>
  <p>
    When you connect one of our applications (such as Rundown) to your CRM or marketing platform
    (for example, LeadConnector), the application accesses certain data from your account in order to provide its features.
    This section explains what we access and how we handle it.
  </p>

  <h3>What we access</h3>
  <p>
    With your authorization (via OAuth), we access the account and performance data needed to generate reports —
    for example: contacts and leads, calls and appointments, pipeline/opportunity data, and lead/traffic sources.
    We request read-only access and do not modify data in your connected account.
  </p>

  <h3>How we use it</h3>
  <p>
    We use this data solely to generate the reports and summaries you request within the application.
    To produce plain-English narratives, report metrics are processed by trusted third-party AI providers
    acting as our sub-processors under confidentiality obligations; this data is not used to train their models.
  </p>

  <h3>What we don't do</h3>
  <p>
    We do not sell, rent, or share your data with third parties for their own purposes, and we do not use it
    for anything other than providing the service to you.
  </p>

  <h3>Storage &amp; retention</h3>
  <p>
    We store only the minimum data needed to operate the service (such as access tokens and generated reports).
    We delete your data within 30 days of disconnection or upon request.
  </p>

  <h3>Your control</h3>
  <p>
    You can disconnect the application at any time, which revokes our access.
    To request export or deletion of your data, contact <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.
  </p>

  <h3>Security</h3>
  <p>
    We protect your data with industry-standard measures, including encryption of access credentials in transit and at rest.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party services</h2>
  <p>
    Our products may use trusted service providers for authentication, hosting, analytics, payment processing,
    and file processing. These providers are used only as needed to operate the service.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${PRIVACY_EMAIL}`}>{PRIVACY_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
</Legal>
